course: dictionary
lesson: 13065
title: The cat family
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Scientists sort living things into groups. A felid is any animal in the cat family, called Felidae. «The vet said the kitten is a felid, just like the tiger at the zoo.» A kitten and a tiger are both felids, even though one is small and one is huge.
explain: Felid is a science word. Everyday English says «cat» or «wild cat» instead. «The big felids hunt at night, when their keen eyes work best.» Here big felids means large members of the cat family, such as lions and cheetahs.
explain: Feline is the adjective, so it describes things. «The feline stretch of the sleepy tabby showed how supple it was.» Feline means like a cat. If you can swap in the word cat-like and the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: A felid is any member of the cat family, Felidae.
fact: Felids include pet cats, lions, tigers, lynxes and cheetahs.
fact: Felids are meat-eaters with sharp claws, keen eyes and whiskers.
fact: «Felid» is a scientific word; everyday English says «cat» or «wild cat».
fact: «Feline» is the adjective, meaning like a cat or belonging to the cat family.
exercise: «The lynx is a felid with tufted ears and big paws.» What is a felid? | A fish with fins | *A member of the cat family | A bird of prey | A plant that grows in water
exercise: Which animals are felids? | *Lions, tigers and pet cats | Frogs and toads | Dogs, wolves and foxes | Horses and cows
exercise: «The feline stretch of the sleepy tabby showed how supple it was.» What does feline mean here? | Very loud | *Like a cat | Like a fish | Like a dog
test: «Felids are meat-eaters with sharp claws.» Which feature do felids have? | Hooves | *Sharp claws | Shells | Long trunks
test: Ben says a cheetah is a felid. Is he right? | *Yes, a cheetah is in the cat family | No, cheetahs are birds | No, cheetahs are plants | No, cheetahs are fish
exam: Which science word means a member of the cat family? | Canine | Bovine | *Felid | Equine
